depends: retry the git clone that builds a source bundle.

simplybs fetches a git-kind source by trying its bundle mirrors first and,
when those fail, cloning the upstream repository and making the bundle
itself (utils/git.go createBundleFromRepo). The mirror path is expected to
fail -- static.mrcyjanek.net resets the connection routinely -- so the
clone is the path that actually runs, and it had no retry of any kind.

DownloadFile's fifteen attempts cover only the HTTP archive kinds. One
dropped connection on the clone therefore failed the whole target:

    Cloning into '.../llvm-project.bundle.clone.tmp'...
    error: 7656 bytes of body are still expected
    fetch-pack: unexpected disconnect while reading sideband packet
    fatal: early EOF
    fatal: fetch-pack: invalid index-pack output
    build.go:115: Failed to download source: failed to clone repository

llvm-project is ~2.2 GiB over 850k objects and is cloned for every target
that needs a cross toolchain, so a transfer long enough to be interrupted
is the normal case rather than bad luck. Under `docker build` the failed
RUN layer is discarded, so that one flake threw away the target's entire
toolchain build and left the next run to start over.

Retry five times. git cannot resume a packfile transfer, so each attempt
starts from zero and the partial clone has to be removed first: git clone
refuses a destination that is not empty, and the failed attempt leaves one
behind because the existing RemoveAll is deferred to function exit.

This does not paper over a dead network. The build sets
http.lowSpeedLimit/http.lowSpeedTime, so a stalled transfer aborts in
seconds and is retried, and five consecutive failures still stop the build
with the underlying git error attached.

--- a/simplybs/utils/git.go
+++ b/simplybs/utils/git.go
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 	"os/exec"
 	"path/filepath"
 	"strings"
+	"time"
 
 	"github.com/mrcyjanek/simplybs/utils/download"
 )
@@ -105,12 +106,35 @@
 	tempDir := bundlePath + ".clone.tmp"
 	defer RemoveAll(tempDir)
 
-	log.Printf("Cloning repository from %s", url)
-	cloneCmd := exec.Command("git", "clone", url, tempDir)
-	cloneCmd.Stdout = os.Stdout
-	cloneCmd.Stderr = os.Stderr
-	if err := cloneCmd.Run(); err != nil {
-		return fmt.Errorf("failed to clone repository: %w", err)
+	// A large repository loses its connection near the end often enough that
+	// one attempt is not a build strategy: llvm-project is ~2.2 GiB over 850k
+	// objects, and nothing else on this path retries -- DownloadFile's
+	// attempts cover the HTTP archive kinds only.
+	//
+	// Each attempt starts from zero because git cannot resume a packfile
+	// transfer, and the partial clone has to be removed first: git clone
+	// refuses a non-empty destination, and the RemoveAll above is deferred to
+	// function exit so it has not run yet.
+	const cloneAttempts = 5
+	var cloneErr error
+	for attempt := 1; attempt <= cloneAttempts; attempt++ {
+		if attempt > 1 {
+			log.Printf("Clone attempt %d/%d for %s", attempt, cloneAttempts, url)
+			time.Sleep(10 * time.Second)
+		}
+		RemoveAll(tempDir)
+
+		log.Printf("Cloning repository from %s", url)
+		cloneCmd := exec.Command("git", "clone", url, tempDir)
+		cloneCmd.Stdout = os.Stdout
+		cloneCmd.Stderr = os.Stderr
+		if cloneErr = cloneCmd.Run(); cloneErr == nil {
+			break
+		}
+		log.Printf("Clone of %s failed: %v", url, cloneErr)
+	}
+	if cloneErr != nil {
+		return fmt.Errorf("failed to clone repository after %d attempts: %w", cloneAttempts, cloneErr)
 	}
 
 	log.Printf("Creating branches for refs: %v", refs)
